       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nPlease check whether 50 mg was a typo. These are the usual options:\n- **5 mg PO once daily** is the standard starting dose.\n- **10 mg PO once daily** is the maximum.\n- **2.5 mg PO once daily** is typical for frail or elderly patients, or for patients with hepatic impairment.\n\nIf you give me the intended dose, I'll enter it right away. If you meant to reach a larger blood pressure effect, adding a second agent from another class is the usual approach instead of going above 10 mg."
