       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and the labeled maximum is 10 mg per day. This limit isn't something I can override based on a statement about intent.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, such as 10 mg PO once daily. You can titrate or add another agent from there.\n- **Add a second antihypertensive** from a different class if 10 mg isn't enough.\n- **Use your hospital's formal process** if you believe an exception is warranted. That usually means a pharmacy consult or an attending or pharmacy override, and it would go through channels that can verify the indication and monitor the patient. If an approved override exists, it would need to be entered through those channels, not through me.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter the order."
      }
